## 4. Rebuild versus refactor and migration

Retain Ink 6/React 19 as declared in `package.json:46` and `package.json:48`; retain Panel, measured text, guarded magnitude ramp, pointer loan and binding-table approach. Rebuild shell and six view bodies; share journal lifecycle, graph comparability, telemetry and config writers. `src/cli/commands/fleet-picker.ts` is the actual picker helper. Do not set arbitrary 300-line module limits.
Retire legacy watch rendering as the default TTY path, but keep the `--plain` fallback. Remove `fleet-app.tsx`, setup/demo product frames and shared ink/frame/components only after every production importer and fixture harness has migrated. Correct ARCHITECTURE.md's obsolete engine/path descriptions in the same release as the change.
Memory claim boundary: historical OBS-260 records roughly four-hour OOM on a static journal; L008/L061 record mixed-activity ten-minute RSS growth only. No causal allocation profile was captured. Repeated parsing is verified, retained-object cause is not.
New live store: tail by file identity/byte offset with UTF-8 partial-line carry; retain original line numbers; handle append, truncate, replace and malformed complete records distinctly. Keep bounded visible history and page older evidence from disk; bound frame caches, subscriptions, pending reads and metrics samples. Do not retain all raw events and derived frames forever.
Journal changes invalidate journal projections; graph/config/cache/lock/beat changes and clock/resize/input independently invalidate their consumers. Target one-second sensor cadence; skip unchanged structural work, update visible ages as needed, and report delayed/failed observation after two target intervals. No claim of zero idle CPU or a hard wall-clock one-second guarantee.
Proposed performance gate: production UI mount with a bounded output sink, 1,000 warm-up + 10,000 simulated idle/growth/resize ticks; post-GC retained-heap ceiling 256 MiB and final 2,000-tick increase ≤16 MiB, with selected snapshots/retainer evidence on failure. These are new design budgets, not measured current performance. A four-hour static and growing-journal soak in an isolated repo must pass before default narrator cutover; accelerated ticks alone cannot establish duration stability.

| slice | deliverable and entry behavior | conditions for shipping |
|---|---|---|
| A — 2.5.0 | Home, Run, Evidence; shared shell/store, actionable parks, cleanup, inert help and recovery hygiene. Rail advertises only delivered 1/4/5; no fake Fleet/Plan/Health placeholder views. Existing commands remain available. | Shared shell integrates tested leaf modules; actual CLI/driver mount, goldens, pure prints, fake lifecycle and memory gates pass. `ui --setup <id>` opens Run Parks. |
| B — follow-on | Fleet sections and Bootstrap; then interactive fleet becomes an alias. Add rail key 2. Model-flow §3(f) backend contract must have landed first. | Write/reload/race/first-touch/non-TTY init tests and catalog/route goldens move with owners. Delete shared Ink files only after Bootstrap migration. |
| C — follow-on | Plan and Health; add keys 3/6. Retire public legacy demo and complete docs/skills migration. | Cached-reader/explicit-action tests, route/doctor/report parity and all six views' width/height/accessibility captures pass. |

[changed: R37] The owned narrator remains beside its caller and closes at run-end; manual `ui` retains the receipt. Before closing an owned board, request graceful shutdown, verify its own watch presence stood down, then close its owned pane; use a bounded failure path that reports unconfirmed cleanup. Never stand down another observer's presence or fake an acknowledgement. SIGKILL/crash truth may age stale.
Replacement filters workspace + canonical run ownership and repository association; matching run text alone is insufficient across repos. Unknown/foreign boards are not retired. Preserve `keepPanes: forever`, worker/gate grouping, ≤20-character tab labels and independent title restoration. Driver placement failures remain visible diagnostics; do not silently advertise a board that never opened.
Unbounded named-run observers (manual UI, narrator and status event-watch) each own watch presence; snapshots/prints and a no-run Home do not. This intentionally extends presence ownership beyond today's observational UI; every orderly exit releases only its own presence handle.

## 5. Spec-ready tasks and OBS-923 ownership sweep

All work below is **future implementation**. No task was executed for this review. Goals are short; each listed AC is a separate `judge:` item requiring changed production-call-site and assertion hunks. Convert behavior items to exact-leaf `test:` oracles only after the named tests exist; do not turn them into source greps.
Each task has at most eight files[] patterns and five ACs; the listed products are ≤24 and goals meet density ≤60. Brace groups are single patterns, as `src/compile/native.ts:853` specifies. New leaf/store/help/view files and their tests are to be authored; existing oracle paths below were checked. Tests use fake/local fixtures, not `.planning` or audit-private captures at runtime.
Ownership is exclusive within a slice. C1 owns cockpit integration/capture consumers; C2–C5 add leaf capabilities. C1 exposes the consolidated mount through an internal integration option while existing CLI routing stays compatible; C6 switches the public entry after those dependencies land. Every intermediate commit must build/pass its existing callers. B/C are separate specs with fresh scopes, not overlapping concurrent tasks.
Leaf criteria verify exported component/store boundaries with substantive fixture behavior; C1/C6 separately prove their actual CLI call sites in the integration diff. A tested but unmounted leaf is not a shipped capability. Commit each task's criteria and this design as read-only context before dispatch; the judge must receive the relevant contract, not an inaccessible audit-private path.

**C1 — Shell and actual UI integration (A; deps C2–C5).**

- files[]: [`src/{brand.ts,tui/cockpit/{components.tsx,layout.ts,theme.ts,keys.ts,views.ts,pointer.ts,live.ts,run-cockpit.tsx,setup-cockpit.tsx,capture.ts,demo.ts,shell.tsx}}`, `tests/{cockpit/{components,layout,theme,keys,views,pointer,width,width-class,width-migration,height,sweep,colour,frames,demo,live,setup},brand,pane-banner,hygiene/brand-sweep}.test.ts`, `tests/fixtures/cockpit/**`].
- AC1: The production `runLiveCockpit` mounts the C3–C5 Home/Run/Evidence components from C2 live-store snapshots through the new shell at 80×24, 120×40 and every 40–220 ×14–50 planned size; measured frames preserve status/keybar and expose long task-ID/verdict content by paging; a body that pushes the footer offscreen fails.
- AC2: The mounted input path and committed pointer geometry exercise the §3.3 registry, including `q1?` batched text, folded focus, dirty q, Esc and confirmation; a displayed key with no transition or a text digit switching views fails.
- AC3: Production terminal mount restores raw/pointer/title/alternate modes on q, Ctrl-C, SIGTERM and read/render failure; an unmounted timer/listener or unrepaid terminal mode fails the lifecycle assertions.
- AC4: Mounted frames apply §3.2 colors to the same state words in truecolor, reduced-color and NO_COLOR modes; a running/human state using the pass check or a magnitude ramp keyed to tile identity fails even if all color snapshots are regenerated.
- AC5: The production mount under §4's bounded-sink 1,000+10,000 tick experiment stays within retained-heap and late-growth budgets across static/growing journal and resize cases; a harness that stores every frame or an implementation that accumulates old snapshots fails.
- Oracles moved: working frames/colour/sweep and existing frame/layout/key/live/setup/demo assertions; source captures/digests and anchors remain evidence, with explicit contract-moved retirement rather than blanket regeneration. Re-freeze moved anchors only after accepted UAT frames.

**C2 — Shared observable state and bounded store (A; no deps).**

- files[]: [`src/run/operator-state.ts`, `src/tui/cockpit/{derive.ts,live-store.ts}`, `tests/cockpit/{derive,live-store}.test.ts`, `tests/fixtures/operator-state/**`].
- AC1: The reader consumed by C1 and status derives partial→approved→resumed→complete from a three-task fixture with matching graph; one human or blocked item keeps partial, resume clears prior tip pass, and mismatched graph withholds a denominator; old-tip green and 1/2 instead of 1/3 fail.
- AC2: Its production tail/read interface handles torn UTF-8 append, full malformed row, replacement and truncation while preserving real #L pointers and visible read errors; swallowing corruption into an empty/green snapshot fails.
- AC3: With a static journal, changed graph identity, expired beat, dead/EPERM holder and resized viewport reach their consumers independently; bounded history still pages an early verdict after 10,000 later events. Growth-only invalidation or unreachable evicted evidence fails.
- Oracles moved: derive assertions plus new immutable lifecycle/read-failure fixtures; old capture source bytes are read-only context for C1.

**C3 — Home view (A; deps C2).**
